  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Physics — Computational Science Track (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] A physics major must complete the foundation courses ( PHYS 101 , PHYS 150 , ASTR 102 , PHYS 206 / PHYS 226 , PHYS 207 / PHYS 227 , PHYS 221 , PHYS 309 , PHYS 331 , MATH 171 , MATH 172 , MATH 221 , MATH 308 ) with a grade of C or better and have a 2.0 cumulative GPA before taking non-foundation upper-level physics courses.\n[grid1 fn2] Any course in this category from the approved University Core Curriculum list of courses.\n[grid1 fn3] PHYS 327 is an approved University Writing course.\n[grid1 fn4] PHYS 328 is an approved University Communication course.\n[grid1 fn5] Electives should be chose in consultation with the student's advisor. Three hours must be in the area of International and Cultural Diversity, and three hours must be in the area of Cultural Discourse. These may be in addition to other University Core Curriculum courses, or, if a course in this category satisfies another area of the Core, it can be used to meet both requirements. Electives may be selected from any 100-499 course not used elsewhere, except ENGL 103 ; MATH 100-148, 165-166, 365-366; PHYS 201 , PHYS 202 .\n[grid1 fn6] Any upper-division course in geo/life/physical sciences, mathematics/statistics or engineering (except 485/491).",
